// Farewells: what a pony says back when you say "See you later." - then the conversation closes.
// Like greetings, they only speak (and run effects); replies and jumps don't belong here.
// One is picked among those whose "when:" holds, by weight - the more particular, the heavier.
//
// PLACEHOLDER LINES - a scaffold showing the shape; every line here is meant to be rewritten.


=== bye
start: farewell
{pony}: See you, {player}!
    or: Bye for now!
    or: Take care!

=== night
start: farewell
weight: 3
when: time_of_day(night)
{pony}: Get home safe, okay?

=== bat_pony_bedtime
start: farewell
weight: 4
when: species(bat_pony), time_of_day(night)
// A bat pony's "night" is everyone else's daytime - they're off to bed.
{pony}: *yawns* Finally, bedtime. Night, {player}.

=== close_friend
start: farewell
weight: 4
when: fondness >= high
{pony}: Come back soon, okay? I mean it!

=== cranky
start: farewell
weight: 3
when: personality(cranky)
{pony}: Yeah, yeah. Go on.

=== peppy
start: farewell
weight: 3
when: personality(peppy)
{pony}: Bye bye! This was the BEST!

=== grieving_pony
start: farewell
weight: 8
when: mood(grief, clear)
{pony}: ...Thanks for stopping by.

=== grieving_player
start: farewell
weight: 8
when: player.mood(grief, clear)
{pony}: Take care of yourself, {player}. Really.

=== rain
start: farewell
weight: 2
when: raining
{pony}: Stay dry out there!
